    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39966" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικωμ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rush on</i> or <i>in with a party of revellers</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				26.1.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				43
			</span></i>: generally, <i>make a riotous assault</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					982
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					881
				</span></i>
			; <i>go careering about</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὰς πόλεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					950a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὴν</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκίαν τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.772f
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτύχημα Σπαρτιάταις
				-εκώμασεν</span> Chor.in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Jahrb.</u>
				9.177
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be visited by a reveller</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pyrrh.</u>
				13
			</span></i>.</div>
